        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Echelon's two real advantages are price and the fold.
            <strong class="text-white">It genuinely undercuts Peloton on both hardware and
            membership</strong>, and the Stride folds close to flat rather than upward — which is
            the difference between a treadmill in a spare room and one in a bedroom.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Run the five-year total before comparing anything, and confirm in writing what the console
            does if you stop paying. If the answer is "not much" and you are not certain about the
            classes,
            <a href="/best-treadmills-without-subscriptions/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">a plain machine</a>
            will cost less across five years and still be working in ten.
          </p>
